  "//": [
    "derive(TypeVisitable[_Generic]) / derive(TypeFoldable[_Generic]) in tools/codegen/types.ts (sets with `derive_type_fold`): the impls of types",
    "the generator does not derive. `trivial`: `TrivialTypeTraversalImpls!` (rustc_type_ir/src/macros.rs, rustc_middle/src/ty/structural_impls.rs",
    "TrivialTypeTraversalImpls / TrivialTypeTraversalAndLiftImpls), plus fieldless derived enums of crates outside the sets (mir BinOp / UnOp,",
    "abstract_const::CastKind: their derived visit is `output()` and fold the value itself). Keys are item keys of a generated set or",
    "type-map paths. `types`: fn names (`$k` = the impls of type argument k, passed after the visitor / folder), `transparent` = the",
    "impl of the type argument (`&T`, `Box<T>`, `Arc<T>`: TS has no box), keys `(T, U)` / `(A, B, C)` / `[T]` / `[T; N]` for tuples,",
    "slices and arrays. A missing `try_fold`/`fold` means upstream has no TypeFoldable impl (a derive over it has an unsatisfiable",
    "where-clause; the generated fn calls `unported`).",
    "`module`: rustc_type_ir fold.ts, the facade of the traversal traits (fold.ts / visit.ts), the impl fn types, the",
    "`TrivialTypeTraversalImpls!` fns (macros.ts) and the container impls of visit.rs / fold.rs; `import`: the module of an",
    "interned type's impls (its type's module, else the module of the upstream file holding the impl; merge-w13)."
  ],
